course: dictionary
lesson: 13190
title: Frothing: bubbles, foam and feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one to use. Frothing is one of these words. «The waves were frothing against the rocks.» Waves are water, so frothing means full of tiny white bubbles, like foam.
explain: «The cook was frothing the milk for the hot chocolate.» Milk does not get angry or excited, so the clue is the milk and the hot chocolate. Frothing here means making the milk into bubbles. Try it: the cook was making the milk into foam. That fits.
explain: «The referee was frothing with rage at the unfair goal.» Rage means fierce anger, so frothing with rage means being extremely angry. This is an informal phrase, so it is a picture of how the person looks, not a real foam on their mouth.
fact: Frothing means making or having lots of tiny bubbles, like foam.
fact: Frothing can also describe foamy spit coming out of an animal's or person's mouth, which can be a sign of illness.
fact: If you see a dog frothing at the mouth, it may be ill: keep your hands away and tell an adult.
fact: «Frothing with rage» is an informal way to say someone is extremely angry or excited.
fact: Frothing happens when air is trapped in a liquid, such as when you shake a fizzy drink or whisk egg whites.
exercise: «The sea was frothing against the rocks.» What does frothing mean here? | Very quiet and still | Freezing cold | Dark and muddy | *Full of tiny bubbles, like foam
exercise: «The coffee machine is frothing the milk.» What is happening to the milk? | *It is turning into lots of tiny bubbles | It is turning into ice | It is being poured down the sink
exercise: «The coach was frothing with rage at the referee.» What does frothing with rage suggest? | *The coach is extremely angry | The coach is lost | The coach is very tired
test: «Shake the fizzy drink and it starts frothing.» Why does the drink froth when you shake it? | The sugar turns into water | The bottle gets heavier | *Air gets trapped in the liquid and makes bubbles | It gets colder and turns to ice
test: The vet said, «The dog is frothing at the mouth, so keep your hands away.» What might this mean? | The dog is hungry for dinner | The dog is very happy and wants a walk | The dog wants a bath | *The dog may be ill
exam: Which meaning of frothing fits «a frothing cup of hot chocolate»? | Very angry | Very dark | *Covered in tiny bubbles, like foam | Very old
